WEBVTT

00:36.161 --> 00:38.955
WE ARE ALL TRYING HERE

00:48.631 --> 00:50.258
I should've fallen in love.

00:51.342 --> 00:53.636
Instead of struggling
to make words come together,

00:54.387 --> 00:55.680
I should've fallen in love.

00:57.515 --> 00:59.225
The words I once forced together

00:59.726 --> 01:02.520
are now pouring out faster
than I can contain them.

01:03.938 --> 01:06.941
It feels like an engine inside me
has just started.

01:07.025 --> 01:07.901
Vroom.

01:09.778 --> 01:11.654
It feels like everything

01:12.155 --> 01:13.740
is working out on its own.

01:13.823 --> 01:14.783
Vroom.

01:15.533 --> 01:18.078
Who knew I had
such a powerful engine inside me?

01:19.079 --> 01:20.622
I should've fallen in love.

01:22.082 --> 01:23.917
Why didn't you tell me you've got a girl?

01:30.673 --> 01:31.841
Hey, I think it's true.

01:32.842 --> 01:35.637
Not long ago, someone threw a rock
through the window at Agit.

01:36.221 --> 01:37.764
Apparently, Eun-a was behind it.

01:37.847 --> 01:38.807
Why would she do that?

01:38.890 --> 01:41.267
Remember when Gyeong-se
posted crap about you in the group chat

01:41.351 --> 01:42.435
and you two were fighting?

01:42.519 --> 01:44.103
Apparently, that's when she did it.

01:49.984 --> 01:51.402
Isn't Eun-a so cool?

02:26.396 --> 02:27.480
Holy shit!

02:30.859 --> 02:32.694
When are you going to get married?

02:34.696 --> 02:38.575
The only girls in my life were those
who dreaded sitting next to me in class

02:39.492 --> 02:41.202
until a woman
as shiny as a blade walked in.

02:42.745 --> 02:44.622
There's nothing I wouldn't do now.

02:45.331 --> 02:46.666
What would you like me to do?

02:47.709 --> 02:49.335
Who should I kill for you?

02:51.379 --> 02:53.381
I really don't understand you.

02:53.464 --> 02:55.758
How could you like a guy
like Hwang Dong-man?

02:56.342 --> 02:58.386
Don't try to understand.
You don't have to.

02:58.469 --> 03:00.179
Why do you keep trying to understand it?

03:00.263 --> 03:01.180
Are you a clarity freak?

03:01.264 --> 03:04.475
When I say I don't understand,
it means I don't like it.

03:04.559 --> 03:05.643
That's what I'm saying.

03:06.436 --> 03:09.856
Why don't you just say you don't like it,
instead of saying you don't understand?

03:10.481 --> 03:11.691
Acting like you're nice.

03:12.483 --> 03:15.111
I'd rather you be honest
and straightforward.

03:17.322 --> 03:18.448
You keep crossing the line.

03:19.073 --> 03:20.700
You crossed it first.

03:21.451 --> 03:25.246
You know people are fragile,
and that a single glance or word

03:25.330 --> 03:27.957
can send them to heaven or hell.

03:28.666 --> 03:29.959
But you still mock me

03:30.793 --> 03:31.628
and sigh at me.

03:35.632 --> 03:36.674
I won't stand for it.

03:39.594 --> 03:40.428
Hey.

03:43.014 --> 03:44.933
As you can see, I've got thick hair.

03:45.016 --> 03:48.353
If you want to grab my hair and fight me,
you'd better be ready to lose a finger.

03:54.567 --> 03:55.610
-Goodbye.
-Thank you.

04:07.997 --> 04:09.123
Did you know?

04:10.166 --> 04:12.001
I even envy the telephone pole

04:12.085 --> 04:13.836
in front of your house

04:14.504 --> 04:16.673
and that smug little "We sell gimbap" sign

04:16.756 --> 04:19.634
hanging from your window bars.

04:20.802 --> 04:24.597
If only I could watch over you all day
like that pole,

04:25.181 --> 04:29.936
or hang from your window all day
like that sign…

04:30.019 --> 04:31.437
WE SELL GIMBAP

04:32.146 --> 04:33.481
I wish I could blow myself up

04:34.190 --> 04:35.650
like the big bang,

04:35.733 --> 04:38.528
so everything around you would be me.

04:40.363 --> 04:41.197
Especially,

04:42.198 --> 04:43.741
that damn gimbap lying on its back

04:43.825 --> 04:46.452
getting gently pressed and rolled
with your hands.

04:47.954 --> 04:49.664
If I could be that gimbap…

04:50.873 --> 04:52.625
Eun-a!

04:57.338 --> 04:58.214
How cozy.

05:35.626 --> 05:40.673
You know, I could spend days imagining
punishing someone or plotting revenge.

05:41.257 --> 05:43.092
I get into the zone and stay up all night.

05:43.718 --> 05:44.802
I even forget to breathe.

05:45.678 --> 05:48.931
But happy imaginations don't last long
before they fall apart.

05:49.932 --> 05:50.850
Why is that?

05:52.101 --> 05:53.603
Is it because I haven't really been happy?

05:56.022 --> 05:58.775
When it falls apart, I get so anxious.

05:59.358 --> 06:01.569
I think I'll stay anxious
until I find success.

06:06.157 --> 06:07.742
Is your brother at home?

06:13.498 --> 06:15.458
He went to Daegwallyeong

06:15.541 --> 06:16.542
to harvest napa cabbage.

06:17.293 --> 06:19.462
Napa cabbage. That's funny.

06:21.422 --> 06:23.299
When there's no welding work,
he does other things.

06:24.383 --> 06:25.426
That's good.

06:27.678 --> 06:29.347
Why are you suddenly asking about him?

06:34.143 --> 06:36.771
My grandmother made some braised kimchi,

06:36.854 --> 06:38.147
so I thought I'd drop some off.

06:39.357 --> 06:40.775
For both of you to enjoy.

06:56.165 --> 06:57.500
Then…

06:57.583 --> 06:58.501
Then…

06:59.085 --> 07:00.837
do you want to eat together?

07:00.920 --> 07:02.505
Do you want to eat together?

07:04.340 --> 07:06.175
DO YOU WANT TO EAT TOGETHER?

07:07.802 --> 07:08.636
Sounds great!

07:10.596 --> 07:11.430
Sounds good.

07:58.019 --> 07:59.061
Careful, it's hot.

08:17.246 --> 08:18.581
Oh, come on!

08:22.627 --> 08:24.921
You said you were harvesting napa cabbage,
and you'd be gone all week!

08:25.505 --> 08:26.797
I said I was going next week.

08:28.716 --> 08:30.718
You've already been drinking?

08:31.761 --> 08:34.055
You could've at least cleaned the place.

08:34.138 --> 08:35.306
Just look at this mess.

08:43.606 --> 08:44.774
Hello.

08:47.818 --> 08:49.195
Releasing steam.

09:09.215 --> 09:10.466
Are those matching watches?

09:14.345 --> 09:16.013
Why are they flashing red?

09:17.974 --> 09:18.849
Jin-man.

09:19.517 --> 09:21.477
Don't just drink. Have some food too.

09:22.436 --> 09:24.522
Show some appreciation
for the person who brought it.

09:39.954 --> 09:41.038
What's your purpose in life?

09:46.669 --> 09:47.587
What about you?

09:47.670 --> 09:49.171
What's your purpose in life?

09:59.807 --> 10:01.684
What kind of person do you want to be?

10:02.268 --> 10:03.644
I'm not talking about being successful.

10:04.854 --> 10:07.148
A lot of successful people are idiots.

10:07.898 --> 10:09.650
"This is the kind of person I want to be."

10:10.693 --> 10:11.569
That kind of purpose.

10:14.322 --> 10:15.740
Just eat. It's okay.

10:22.038 --> 10:23.122
A strong mother.

10:27.793 --> 10:30.630
Yeah, I'm going to become a strong mother.

10:32.673 --> 10:35.259
Not the type of strength
that comes from money or connections.

10:37.303 --> 10:39.764
I want to become a mother
who remains calm in any situation.

10:42.600 --> 10:44.393
The kind who stands steady at the center

10:45.186 --> 10:46.103
so that

10:47.188 --> 10:50.232
her presence puts everyone
around her at ease.

10:50.941 --> 10:52.443
That's the kind of woman I want to be.

10:58.866 --> 11:00.076
Like my grandmother.

11:16.133 --> 11:16.967
What's wrong?

11:17.968 --> 11:18.886
What is it?

11:22.932 --> 11:23.766
What is it?

11:36.612 --> 11:37.822
Name?

11:39.407 --> 11:40.616
Byeon Eun-a.

11:40.699 --> 11:41.534
Eun-a.

11:58.092 --> 11:59.218
Thank you.

12:03.931 --> 12:07.017
DAYS LIKE THIS, DAYS LIKE THAT
POEMS BY HWANG JIN-MAN

12:07.101 --> 12:09.603
TO MS. BYEON EUN-A
I HOPE YOU BECOME A STRONG MOTHER

12:13.607 --> 12:14.733
Thank you.

12:21.740 --> 12:23.242
I'm giving in on everything else!

12:23.325 --> 12:25.494
How much more do I have to compromise?
I won't do it.

12:27.288 --> 12:29.123
-So scrap it?
-Scrap it!

12:29.707 --> 12:33.085
There's no point working with assholes
who boss you around from the start!

12:33.169 --> 12:34.003
Just scrap it!

12:36.881 --> 12:39.091
-Am I really asking for too much?
-Jeez.

12:39.175 --> 12:41.886
I thought things were good
since it was scheduled for streaming.

12:42.636 --> 12:45.473
National Stress Management Department
has been confirmed, right?

12:46.223 --> 12:47.558
It's been confirmed, but…

12:47.641 --> 12:48.893
But what?

12:48.976 --> 12:52.771
They said eight episodes might be too much
for Director Park to write alone,

12:52.855 --> 12:54.273
so they want to bring in another writer.

12:57.818 --> 12:59.695
That was a huge mistake.

12:59.778 --> 13:03.115
They really shouldn't have messed
with his writing.

13:03.908 --> 13:06.202
What is this, a factory?
Two writers don't mean faster writing.

13:06.285 --> 13:09.330
How dare they tell the director
to work with another writer?

13:09.413 --> 13:10.706
They're way out of line.

13:10.789 --> 13:12.625
-Does money give them control over me?
-Yeah, it does.

13:13.209 --> 13:14.960
It's my idea and my screenplay.

13:15.044 --> 13:16.795
If they don't like it,
I can take it somewhere else.

13:16.879 --> 13:17.755
Where, exactly?

13:18.339 --> 13:20.841
Go ahead, see if anyone
will offer you tens of billions of won.

13:22.343 --> 13:24.678
They can't even ask for that
when they're putting up tens of billions?

13:24.762 --> 13:26.514
This is your first series.

13:26.597 --> 13:30.392
Is getting help from someone experienced
really something to lose your temper over?

13:30.476 --> 13:31.936
That's what I'm saying.

13:32.019 --> 13:34.688
Why do they think I need help?

13:34.772 --> 13:37.525
-It's because they think I'm lacking!
-Seriously?

13:38.192 --> 13:39.944
As if you've never… Oh gosh.

13:40.027 --> 13:41.487
Who do they think they are?
I'm the director.

13:43.739 --> 13:45.950
I'm writing the whole thing,
from start to finish!

13:46.033 --> 13:47.701
Only Park Gyeong-se is allowed.

13:49.119 --> 13:50.788
These so-called directors
are all the same.

13:51.413 --> 13:54.667
Every single one of them
is just full of insecurity.

13:54.750 --> 13:56.544
You're all desperate to make it big,

13:56.627 --> 14:00.297
but you have this pathetic idea
that accepting help makes you weak

14:00.381 --> 14:01.882
and ruins your perfect image.

14:04.552 --> 14:06.762
Meanwhile, I'm wondering
how I'll pay the staff this month

14:06.845 --> 14:08.097
or how I'll pay the rent.

14:08.180 --> 14:11.350
I'm desperately looking
for any bit of help I can get.

14:11.433 --> 14:14.895
I'd welcome any help I can get
with open arms.

14:14.979 --> 14:16.105
I'd kill for some help!

14:23.320 --> 14:24.238
Listen carefully.

14:26.824 --> 14:27.700
Gyeong-se.

14:28.742 --> 14:29.577
You're old.

14:32.371 --> 14:33.289
You're outdated.

14:41.881 --> 14:43.048
You've been outdated for a long time.

14:43.132 --> 14:46.677
How many of your films start strong
only to fall apart later?

14:47.678 --> 14:50.639
That's why people say
you only ever lick the watermelon.

14:53.350 --> 14:56.520
Covering the losses
of a two-hour film is one thing,

14:56.604 --> 14:58.647
but there's no way to do that
for a series.

14:59.231 --> 15:01.942
If this fails,
there won't be a next time for you.

15:02.443 --> 15:04.612
So take the help.

15:05.362 --> 15:06.363
Take it while you can.

15:07.114 --> 15:08.574
How could you say that to me?

15:11.452 --> 15:12.328
Do you…

15:14.872 --> 15:16.040
even love me?

15:18.208 --> 15:19.501
Twenty years together,

15:19.585 --> 15:23.714
and you're still using outdated lines,
asking me if I love you.

15:23.797 --> 15:24.924
And you still want to write alone?

15:26.342 --> 15:29.011
Saying I don't love you
doesn't make me feel guilty,

15:29.720 --> 15:33.223
and saying that I do
doesn't benefit me at all, okay?

15:34.725 --> 15:36.393
Think this through.

15:37.603 --> 15:41.482
Byeon Eun-a can revive dead scripts,
and now she's backing Hwang Dong-man.

15:42.483 --> 15:45.402
Either sit there as the director
who flopped with Sister Vengeance

15:45.486 --> 15:47.571
and watch Hwang Dong-man
debut with a bang,

15:48.072 --> 15:49.990
or hurry up and put out something new.

15:51.408 --> 15:52.242
That's it.

16:07.341 --> 16:09.093
I'm sorry. I didn't know Jin-man was home.

16:09.802 --> 16:10.678
I bet it was uncomfortable.

16:11.845 --> 16:12.846
It was nice.

16:14.098 --> 16:16.433
I didn't think I had a purpose in life.

16:17.601 --> 16:20.729
But when he asked me out of the blue,
the answer just came out.

16:24.566 --> 16:26.151
Sometimes when you speak,

16:27.069 --> 16:29.530
it feels like our surroundings
turn into a vacuum.

16:30.781 --> 16:33.075
Earlier, when you were talking about
wanting to be a strong mother,

16:33.158 --> 16:35.035
all of a sudden, it felt like…

16:36.870 --> 16:38.205
the three of us were in space.

16:39.456 --> 16:40.874
And eating in space.

16:43.168 --> 16:45.921
I pictured us eating in space,
and it's funny.

16:57.349 --> 16:59.518
It's not a disaster alert message.

16:59.601 --> 17:01.145
It's from the emotion watch company.

17:01.228 --> 17:03.355
"Participant number 4000,

17:03.439 --> 17:05.899
your update is scheduled for Friday."

17:05.983 --> 17:07.151
What?

17:07.234 --> 17:09.737
Number 4000 out of 4000 people.
You're the last one.

17:09.820 --> 17:11.280
I barely made it in.

17:11.363 --> 17:12.614
I'm number 38.

17:14.366 --> 17:15.534
That's a winning hand.

17:17.119 --> 17:18.328
You got in early.

17:19.329 --> 17:20.748
Successful people are always like this.

17:21.373 --> 17:22.332
They always play it safe.

17:22.916 --> 17:25.419
Really? I think number 4000
feels way luckier.

17:25.502 --> 17:27.755
My life is always on the edge.

17:32.468 --> 17:33.802
It feels like winter is coming.

17:34.428 --> 17:36.055
Not a fan of winter?

17:36.138 --> 17:37.514
I like wind, though.

17:38.140 --> 17:40.225
I like the wind regardless of the season.

17:45.272 --> 17:46.148
Yes?

17:48.609 --> 17:49.485
Hello?

17:50.861 --> 17:52.446
Is that you, Si-on?

18:03.540 --> 18:04.416
It's me,

18:05.626 --> 18:06.460
Mom.

18:26.980 --> 18:29.066
-It was a wrong number.
-I see.

18:46.750 --> 18:48.544
The leaves are all falling here,

18:48.627 --> 18:51.088
but isn't it strange that Gangwon-do
still has fresh green napa cabbage?

18:56.510 --> 18:57.344
It's strange.

19:06.478 --> 19:08.438
Which sounds better,
Byeon Si-on or Byeon Eun-a?

19:09.022 --> 19:10.524
Byeon Eun-a is a hundred times better.

19:10.607 --> 19:11.733
Byeon Si-on is over the top.

19:13.110 --> 19:14.111
Are you changing your name?

19:14.611 --> 19:15.612
Nope.

19:15.696 --> 19:17.739
Byeon Eun-a is way better. I mean it.

19:21.243 --> 19:22.161
A long time ago…

19:28.041 --> 19:31.128
Jin-man said you shouldn't
go over the top with people's names.

19:31.753 --> 19:33.255
So he named my niece "Yeong-sil,"

19:34.089 --> 19:35.632
hoping she'd live an easygoing life.

19:37.050 --> 19:39.094
But her last name is "Hwang."

19:39.178 --> 19:40.137
Hwang Yeong-sil.

19:40.762 --> 19:42.222
She's bound for a tough life.

19:44.099 --> 19:45.184
"Yeong-sil."

19:46.476 --> 19:47.644
That's nice.

19:50.689 --> 19:52.482
How old is your niece now?

19:54.985 --> 19:55.861
Probably…

19:57.279 --> 19:58.322
14 years old,

19:59.531 --> 20:00.657
I think.

20:09.750 --> 20:11.126
Oh, let's go.

20:16.048 --> 20:17.090
It's so cold!

20:24.056 --> 20:24.890
Have a good night.

20:26.516 --> 20:27.434
Right.

20:27.517 --> 20:28.727
Good night.

20:28.810 --> 20:29.645
Here you go.

20:54.211 --> 20:55.087
Don't be so smug.

21:09.226 --> 21:10.227
It's Mom.

21:11.270 --> 21:12.229
Call me.

21:25.617 --> 21:26.576
What's going on?

21:27.995 --> 21:29.913
Why are you already drunk
so early in the evening?

21:34.710 --> 21:35.627
Just getting home now?

21:44.845 --> 21:46.305
Hey, hey, hey!

21:49.850 --> 21:50.851
A perfect ten.

21:58.483 --> 21:59.860
So tell me.

21:59.943 --> 22:02.946
Has it been nice and peaceful here
while I was gone?

22:04.031 --> 22:05.282
I have bad news, though.

22:05.365 --> 22:06.408
The peace ends today.

22:11.288 --> 22:13.457
Okay, okay.

22:17.336 --> 22:18.378
I'll accept your apology.

22:25.177 --> 22:26.845
Hey, what's all this?

22:26.928 --> 22:29.765
Oh, how I've missed the taste of home!

22:33.477 --> 22:34.895
Over the past 20 years,

22:35.937 --> 22:39.357
The Eight Club has split up
and gotten back together countless times.

22:40.400 --> 22:42.861
Hey, sit down. You're being distracting.

22:44.321 --> 22:47.699
After dragging Hwang Dong-man back,
we got back together again.

22:47.783 --> 22:49.326
I don't know how many more times

22:49.993 --> 22:51.787
we'll split apart and reunite, but--

22:51.870 --> 22:52.746
Hey, you punk.

22:53.747 --> 22:55.373
We're here because of you,
but you came last.

22:56.208 --> 22:57.375
Sorry.

22:57.459 --> 22:58.335
Damn it.

22:58.418 --> 22:59.628
Hey, go sit over there.

22:59.711 --> 23:01.004
-Next to Gyeong-se.
-No.

23:02.089 --> 23:03.840
-Go.
-No! Why?

23:03.924 --> 23:05.217
Go. Sit next to him!

23:05.300 --> 23:06.384
-Come on!
-Right now.

23:06.468 --> 23:08.595
You'll notice him less
if he's sitting next to you.

23:08.678 --> 23:10.430
-Come on.
-Hurry up and move! Hurry!

23:11.348 --> 23:12.224
Jeez.

23:12.307 --> 23:13.975
Seriously?

23:14.810 --> 23:17.562
These two punks
need to stay out of each other's sight,

23:17.646 --> 23:18.939
or they'll start snarling again.

23:21.775 --> 23:22.859
Oh my.

23:23.610 --> 23:25.278
It's nice not having to see him.

23:25.362 --> 23:28.073
Jeez, is there a way
I don't have to hear his voice either?

23:28.156 --> 23:30.075
Hey, bring me some super glue

23:30.158 --> 23:31.785
so I can plug his ears.

23:32.744 --> 23:36.331
From now on, sit side by side like this
so you can't see each other. Got it?

23:37.165 --> 23:39.126
Who'd have thought
these two used to be best friends?

23:39.209 --> 23:40.836
We weren't best friends.

23:40.919 --> 23:43.547
You think we were best friends
just because we lived together?

23:43.630 --> 23:45.465
Hey. Ormy and Gasmy.

23:45.549 --> 23:46.633
-Hey!
-Come on!

23:47.926 --> 23:49.010
-Jeez.
-Darn it.

23:49.094 --> 23:52.514
You'd be up all night watching movies,
but hesitate to say which ones.

23:52.597 --> 23:56.726
You'd be up all night watching porn,
then come to school with bloodshot eyes.

23:56.810 --> 24:00.272
Hey, who could be better friends
than Ormy and Gasmy?

24:00.355 --> 24:03.483
You two even share a sacred word
as your nicknames.

24:04.109 --> 24:05.861
Anyway, I dare you to fight again.

24:05.944 --> 24:09.447
If you do, I'll dig up your past again.

24:09.531 --> 24:10.907
Got it, Pyramid and Scheme?

24:10.991 --> 24:11.992
-Hey!
-Come on!

24:12.075 --> 24:13.869
-This takes me back.
-They were locked in a room

24:13.952 --> 24:15.579
because of that pyramid scheme.

24:15.662 --> 24:19.499
-Hey, cut it out!
-Let's toast. Come on, let's toast.

24:19.583 --> 24:20.667
Hey!

24:20.750 --> 24:23.420
-Here's to Ormy and Gasmy's reunion!
-Come on!

24:23.503 --> 24:25.839
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

24:29.092 --> 24:31.970
All of you need to write
while you're still young.

24:33.096 --> 24:35.891
When you get old, you can't crap or write.

24:36.641 --> 24:38.059
It's true.

24:38.143 --> 24:39.978
The power it takes to push out crap

24:40.061 --> 24:41.897
is proportional
to the power of creativity.

24:41.980 --> 24:43.690
Back in the day, I thought,

24:45.358 --> 24:46.276
"All right."

24:47.110 --> 24:50.113
"I'll just tear my ass open
and push it out."

24:50.197 --> 24:52.490
If I put my mind to it,
I could force it to come out.

24:53.366 --> 24:55.994
But now, I can't even imagine doing that.

24:56.077 --> 24:57.078
It'll end badly.

24:57.704 --> 24:59.206
It's the same with writing.

24:59.289 --> 25:00.582
Even if I stay up three nights straight,

25:01.583 --> 25:02.417
nothing comes out.

25:04.836 --> 25:08.465
It won't come out
because you're forcing it.

25:08.548 --> 25:10.842
You need to start your engine.

25:10.926 --> 25:12.385
Then it'll come out on its own.

25:12.469 --> 25:14.262
It'll come out while you're sleeping,

25:14.346 --> 25:16.223
or while you're taking a crap.

25:16.306 --> 25:18.016
It'll just pour out nonstop.

25:18.642 --> 25:20.977
We all have an engine inside us.

25:21.978 --> 25:23.396
So how exactly

25:24.189 --> 25:25.398
do you start that engine?

25:26.524 --> 25:29.236
That's the thing. I have no idea.

25:29.319 --> 25:30.320
It just started.

25:31.488 --> 25:33.198
I didn't even know I had one.

25:33.823 --> 25:35.617
He's saying you need to be in love.

25:36.618 --> 25:38.995
No, that's not it. It's something else.

25:39.788 --> 25:41.206
Everyone's got it.

25:41.289 --> 25:43.083
Beethoven had it,

25:43.166 --> 25:44.626
and I have it too.

25:46.002 --> 25:49.881
I read a biography on Beethoven as a kid,
and there was something I didn't get.

25:50.465 --> 25:51.508
While he was composing,

25:51.591 --> 25:54.135
he asked his servant
to bring him some warm milk.

25:54.219 --> 25:56.263
But as he was about to drink it,
he found it was cold.

25:56.346 --> 25:57.764
He was furious and asked,

25:57.847 --> 26:01.059
"I asked for warm milk,
so why is it cold?"

26:01.142 --> 26:02.811
But it turns out,

26:02.894 --> 26:05.063
the servant brought him warm milk,

26:05.146 --> 26:06.648
but he was so focused on composing

26:06.731 --> 26:08.858
that he didn't notice
the milk had gone cold.

26:09.859 --> 26:10.819
That made me wonder,

26:11.319 --> 26:14.197
"How could you not notice something
right next to you?"

26:14.281 --> 26:15.490
But guess what?

26:16.116 --> 26:20.453
I was writing like crazy yesterday
and thought,

26:20.537 --> 26:22.163
"I should get some coffee."

26:22.247 --> 26:23.540
So I got up, but then…

26:26.626 --> 26:27.877
it was already brewed.

26:28.586 --> 26:29.796
And it was cold.

26:30.630 --> 26:31.965
I forgot I had brewed it.

26:33.466 --> 26:35.760
I felt a sense of pride,
like I was on the same level

26:36.511 --> 26:37.595
as Beethoven.

26:37.679 --> 26:38.888
You forgot because it was coffee.

26:38.972 --> 26:40.473
You wouldn't have
if it had been instant noodles.

26:41.057 --> 26:42.434
Goddamn it.

26:42.934 --> 26:44.602
Are you trying to ruin the mood, sir?

26:44.686 --> 26:46.604
You know why we started
hating each other so much?

26:47.856 --> 26:50.442
You could say
it's like hating your own kind.

26:51.026 --> 26:51.901
Both of us

26:52.819 --> 26:53.653
are frivolous.

26:53.737 --> 26:56.323
We're too shallow and can't dive deep.

26:56.406 --> 26:58.450
That's why our writing is full of seaweed,

26:58.533 --> 27:00.452
and not a single abalone or conch.

27:01.703 --> 27:04.497
But now, I'm able to dive deep.

27:05.081 --> 27:06.958
I can even get abalone,

27:07.042 --> 27:10.295
which means we're no longer the same kind.

27:12.464 --> 27:13.465
Bye.

27:22.307 --> 27:23.725
Have some watermelon,

27:23.808 --> 27:26.102
instead of always licking the surface.

27:26.186 --> 27:28.813
You've got to taste the sweetness.

27:37.864 --> 27:39.366
Brace for impact.

27:39.449 --> 27:40.909
Brace for impact.

27:51.419 --> 27:52.420
Just watch.

27:53.171 --> 27:54.672
I'm about to blow up.

28:03.640 --> 28:04.516
It was a good read.

28:06.518 --> 28:10.522
There are so many good lines
you can't help but stop and take them in.

28:10.605 --> 28:13.358
Read it, pick ten expressions you like,
and keep them in mind.

28:14.067 --> 28:15.527
Then at some point,

28:15.610 --> 28:17.570
the right words will come out
at the right time.

28:19.280 --> 28:21.783
Then people will look at you differently.

28:23.910 --> 28:25.787
Did you finish the book
I gave you last time?

28:27.163 --> 28:28.581
Stop looking at your phone.

28:30.417 --> 28:31.918
Another person came forward.

28:32.001 --> 28:34.087
They claim to be
your biological daughter's classmate.

28:37.882 --> 28:39.843
There's even a photo
from when she was young.

28:51.354 --> 28:53.565
THAT SLOPPY GIMBAP
SHE CLEARLY MADE HERSELF…

28:53.648 --> 28:56.109
I STILL THINK ABOUT THAT SAD GIMBAP
AND HOW SHE FORCED IT DOWN

29:16.880 --> 29:19.632
I don't think
we can stay silent any longer.

29:20.216 --> 29:23.344
We should do an exclusive interview
and get an article out today.

29:23.428 --> 29:26.264
Reporter Yeom's on standby
and said to call anytime.

29:26.347 --> 29:29.809
After you return from today's event,
the office will be ready for an interview.

29:29.893 --> 29:31.144
Forget it.

29:31.227 --> 29:32.937
I'll tell them myself.

29:33.021 --> 29:34.898
On live TV, in front of the whole country.

29:34.981 --> 29:37.776
But doing nothing until the award ceremony
won't sit well with the public.

29:37.859 --> 29:40.236
People with nothing better to do

29:40.320 --> 29:43.281
get their entertainment
from watching celebrities crash and burn.

29:43.364 --> 29:44.616
Let them enjoy it for a few more days.

29:48.453 --> 29:50.580
-Thank you for today.
-All right, bye.

29:53.750 --> 29:54.834
Mr. Hwang.

29:55.960 --> 29:57.337
Would you like to grab a bite?

29:57.420 --> 29:59.088
I have to go home and make revisions.

29:59.172 --> 30:00.507
Even an all-nighter won't cut it

30:00.590 --> 30:02.091
if I want to start casting next week.

30:03.343 --> 30:05.804
I finally get to show my screenplay
to actors.

30:06.596 --> 30:09.432
Mr. Hwang, promise you'll invite me
to the premiere.

30:10.892 --> 30:12.602
Bring both your parents.

30:13.186 --> 30:15.396
I'll seat you right in the center,
right next to the cast.

30:15.480 --> 30:16.481
Thank you.

30:16.564 --> 30:17.649
-Let's go.
-Okay.

30:29.202 --> 30:30.036
Mr. Hwang.

30:32.413 --> 30:33.456
You've got this.

30:34.207 --> 30:35.375
You've got this, Myeong-hun!

30:36.793 --> 30:38.002
-See you.
-Goodbye.

31:11.286 --> 31:12.120
Hey.

31:14.706 --> 31:16.666
Days like this are worth living

31:18.543 --> 31:19.627
If you've gone far away

31:20.503 --> 31:21.880
It would be a good day to come back

32:11.304 --> 32:12.221
Jin-man…

34:02.415 --> 34:03.791
CATERING COMPANY OWNER

34:03.875 --> 34:05.043
I'm sorry.

34:05.126 --> 34:08.880
Something came up at home,
so I can't come to work today.

34:40.078 --> 34:40.912
Where are you going?

34:43.498 --> 34:44.916
Where else? I'm going to work.

36:13.254 --> 36:14.297
-Are they here?
-Yes, sir.

36:25.224 --> 36:26.517
Oh Jeong-hui deserves

36:27.476 --> 36:28.853
whatever shit I want to give her.

36:29.645 --> 36:30.563
That's where she stands.

36:30.646 --> 36:33.566
She can't say a word,
no matter what I say. Why?

36:33.649 --> 36:36.444
She tarnished a blockbuster movie
when her family scandal broke out

36:36.527 --> 36:40.031
and halted post-production
on another finished movie.

36:40.114 --> 36:41.490
But did you know

36:42.950 --> 36:44.994
that Oh Jeong-hui gave me shit instead?

36:45.703 --> 36:47.121
She called first thing this morning

36:48.039 --> 36:52.084
bitching about how I gave her daughter
a crappy screenplay like this.

36:52.710 --> 36:54.003
This is exactly why

36:55.087 --> 36:57.340
I told you not to give screenplays
directly to the actor.

36:58.174 --> 37:02.178
How the hell can the CEO not know
which actor got the screenplay?

37:04.138 --> 37:05.097
I'm sorry, sir.

37:05.723 --> 37:07.808
Get ready to be chewed out by an actor.

37:29.789 --> 37:30.748
It's Jang Mi-ran!

37:31.332 --> 37:32.416
-It's Jang Mi-ran!
-Jang Mi-ran?

37:32.500 --> 37:34.377
-Wow.
-It's Jang Mi-ran.

37:37.004 --> 37:39.924
Right now, this feels like a dream

37:40.007 --> 37:43.886
You and me, dancing together

37:43.970 --> 37:46.889
The feeling is so incredible
It's like art

37:46.973 --> 37:49.433
-Jang Mi-ran!
-Jang Mi-ran!

37:49.517 --> 37:52.687
-Jang Mi-ran!
-Jang Mi-ran!

37:54.855 --> 37:56.524
This way please, Mi-ran.

37:58.484 --> 37:59.610
You're so pretty!

37:59.694 --> 38:01.195
She's seriously pretty.

38:04.490 --> 38:06.701
-Hello.
-Gosh, it's hot.

38:11.289 --> 38:12.581
Can you believe it?

38:13.749 --> 38:16.752
Only 310,000 people watched the movie
I worked my ass off for,

38:17.253 --> 38:19.755
but a video of me half-ass singing
at a wedding got five million views.

38:19.839 --> 38:21.048
Maybe I should quit acting.

38:22.091 --> 38:23.134
Who's this?

38:23.217 --> 38:25.011
This is Producer Byeon Eun-a
from Choi Film.

38:25.094 --> 38:25.970
She's working with me.

38:27.096 --> 38:28.139
Nice to meet you.

38:30.349 --> 38:32.852
With a face like that,
you should be an actor, not a producer.

38:34.395 --> 38:35.896
Never mind. Don't be an actor.

38:37.064 --> 38:38.774
When I was a sophomore in high school,

38:38.858 --> 38:43.237
I went through hell
because I couldn't eat or sleep.

38:43.321 --> 38:46.407
I went to a bunch of hospitals, but no one
could figure out what was wrong.

38:47.033 --> 38:51.120
Then my grandma went to a shaman,
who told her I was chosen by spirits

38:51.203 --> 38:52.455
and destined to be a shaman.

38:53.205 --> 38:56.542
They say a shaman's fate
and an actor's fate are similar,

38:56.625 --> 38:59.337
so I had to become an actor
if I didn't want to become a shaman.

39:01.172 --> 39:02.506
I should've just become a shaman.

39:03.215 --> 39:04.508
Acting is more exhausting.

39:04.592 --> 39:06.052
At least shamans don't saw off their arms.

39:07.511 --> 39:09.430
I saw off my arm once,
and now every role is the same.

39:09.513 --> 39:12.808
They hack away with an ax
or a pair of scissors.

39:13.392 --> 39:14.560
Director Lee Jun-hwan,

39:15.644 --> 39:17.980
I liked you because you looked polished.

39:18.647 --> 39:20.775
So how is it that your writing
is so crappy?

39:25.154 --> 39:26.322
A SCARY WOMAN

39:26.405 --> 39:29.950
You can't use actors like this, all right?

39:30.034 --> 39:31.619
Directors need to reflect on this.

39:38.501 --> 39:40.211
It doesn't matter
if you saw off an arm or a leg.

39:42.588 --> 39:46.634
Do you know the biggest flaw
in the characters you've been playing?

39:47.885 --> 39:49.512
It's that they know
how to use their heads.

39:52.390 --> 39:53.766
But you don't know how to use yours.

39:55.226 --> 39:56.811
Every time I watch you in a movie

39:56.894 --> 40:01.440
and see you act sophisticated,
I lose it because it doesn't suit you.

40:02.024 --> 40:04.693
Why does someone
with such raw, natural appeal in real life

40:05.444 --> 40:08.739
start to use her head
the second she's on camera?

40:09.740 --> 40:14.286
We want a larger-than-life Jang Mi-ran
who can make us burst out laughing.

40:15.204 --> 40:17.706
We don't want to watch someone
who's just like us,

40:17.790 --> 40:20.126
struggling to use their head.

40:25.464 --> 40:26.340
A SCARY WOMAN

40:26.424 --> 40:27.842
This character doesn't use her head,

40:28.801 --> 40:30.344
so she doesn't think things through

40:30.428 --> 40:31.762
or make calculations.

40:32.805 --> 40:33.639
She's someone…

40:35.391 --> 40:37.226
who's driven purely by her heart.

40:39.728 --> 40:41.021
That's what makes her scary.

40:43.774 --> 40:47.194
Isn't this the first role
that fits you perfectly?

40:55.286 --> 40:56.203
Hey.

41:20.561 --> 41:21.937
That bitch is Ax, right?

41:22.021 --> 41:23.481
The one who got screwed
for running her mouth?

41:31.864 --> 41:33.240
Put that crazy bitch on the phone.

41:33.908 --> 41:35.284
Just put her on!

41:44.084 --> 41:44.919
Yes?

41:45.002 --> 41:46.003
Hey.

41:46.795 --> 41:48.214
Answer my calls from now on.

41:48.839 --> 41:51.300
The second you start kissing my ass,
you're done.

41:58.057 --> 41:59.183
What did she say?

41:59.767 --> 42:00.976
I think she'll do it.

42:20.996 --> 42:21.997
Excuse me.

42:23.958 --> 42:26.418
Please answer Ms. Oh Jeong-hui's call.

42:28.295 --> 42:29.129
I really hope

42:30.464 --> 42:31.549
you answer her call today.

42:33.926 --> 42:34.927
Please.

43:29.982 --> 43:31.859
HANKUK UNIVERSITY GRADUATE SCHOOL
KOREAN LITERATURE, HWANG JIN-MAN

44:12.191 --> 44:14.318
BIRTH REGISTRATION
NAME: HWANG YEONG-SIL

44:32.127 --> 44:34.838
NATIONAL CENTER
FOR THE RIGHTS OF THE CHILD

44:42.513 --> 44:43.597
I'm sorry.

44:44.306 --> 44:46.475
We're legally prohibited
from disclosing information

44:46.558 --> 44:48.310
about adoptive parents.

44:49.353 --> 44:50.270
At this point,

44:50.354 --> 44:53.440
your only option is to wait for your niece
to look for her biological parents.

44:54.608 --> 44:57.653
How could she have been adopted
without her father's knowledge?

44:57.736 --> 44:59.113
Even if they were divorced,

44:59.905 --> 45:01.949
how can you do that
without the father's consent?

45:02.533 --> 45:06.203
Records show that the father's whereabouts
were unknown at the time,

45:06.829 --> 45:09.498
so the mother's consent alone
was sufficient.

45:12.084 --> 45:13.669
Can I get her address?

45:14.545 --> 45:16.046
Can't you at least tell me that?

45:18.799 --> 45:21.051
It's too harsh not to know

45:22.761 --> 45:23.929
where your child lives.

45:31.854 --> 45:33.689
I'm not even hoping for success.

45:34.606 --> 45:35.441
I just

45:36.316 --> 45:38.152
don't want to be miserable.

46:16.315 --> 46:17.232
What is it?

46:18.984 --> 46:20.277
Did your engine die?

46:25.157 --> 46:26.950
Is it better that we all succeed together,

46:28.660 --> 46:30.037
or that we all go down together?

46:30.746 --> 46:32.831
It's easier if we all go down together.

46:35.834 --> 46:38.045
Going down isn't so bad.

46:39.213 --> 46:40.088
As long as we're together.

46:46.887 --> 46:48.430
It's funny, you know.

46:50.265 --> 46:52.434
When I'm deep in my feelings…

46:54.353 --> 46:55.437
I don't hate you.

46:57.648 --> 46:59.733
I don't hate you when I'm really happy.

47:01.818 --> 47:02.653
And I don't hate you

47:03.737 --> 47:05.072
when I feel really sad.

47:42.401 --> 47:44.611
FIVE HUNDRED WON

48:14.683 --> 48:15.809
Yes?

48:18.103 --> 48:19.146
Is that you, Si-on?

48:20.439 --> 48:21.481
This is Eun-a.

48:22.232 --> 48:23.233
Byeon Eun-a.

48:24.484 --> 48:25.819
Why did you change your name?

48:30.866 --> 48:32.701
I didn't know your father had died.

48:33.577 --> 48:35.954
Don't worry anymore. You've got me now.

48:38.415 --> 48:40.626
Now you can do

48:40.709 --> 48:41.960
whatever you want.

48:42.794 --> 48:44.254
If you want,

48:44.838 --> 48:46.715
you can start studying again.

48:48.133 --> 48:49.551
You can even study abroad.

48:50.594 --> 48:52.596
Tell me if there's anywhere
you want to go.

48:53.221 --> 48:54.598
I'll make it happen.

48:54.681 --> 48:55.515
Why?

48:56.808 --> 48:58.310
Are you still ashamed of me?

48:59.811 --> 49:01.813
Do you want me to disappear
somewhere far away?

49:01.897 --> 49:02.898
Or are you

49:03.649 --> 49:04.816
trying to save yourself

49:05.651 --> 49:07.736
by taking back the daughter you abandoned?

49:07.819 --> 49:09.196
I never abandoned you.

49:09.279 --> 49:10.697
It was your father I left.

49:11.531 --> 49:14.576
If I had known he died,
I would've come for you right away.

49:15.243 --> 49:16.912
Because you're no longer
Byeon Jae-su's daughter,

49:17.496 --> 49:18.705
but Oh Jeong-hui's daughter.

49:19.289 --> 49:21.083
I know that you're desperate,

49:21.958 --> 49:24.503
but I have my own memories,
and you have yours.

49:25.462 --> 49:27.172
Don't pretend you're a caring mother.

49:28.757 --> 49:30.175
A nine-year-old kid wanted to hide

49:30.759 --> 49:32.052
the fact that she'd been abandoned,

49:32.135 --> 49:34.304
so she made her own gimbap
for the field trip.

49:34.971 --> 49:37.099
I didn't want anyone to know
that the poor kid was me,

49:37.182 --> 49:39.685
so I even changed my name
and lived a quiet life.

49:40.644 --> 49:41.603
What I'm saying is

49:42.604 --> 49:45.148
don't let anyone find out
that the poor kid Oh Jeong-hui abandoned

49:46.525 --> 49:47.901
is actually me.

49:50.445 --> 49:52.030
I won't let anyone find out either.

50:09.756 --> 50:10.757
We're here, ma'am.

50:30.944 --> 50:33.864
46TH KOREAN FILM AWARDS

50:44.708 --> 50:45.542
Go ahead and leave!

50:45.625 --> 50:48.128
All you've done is leech off my name!

50:57.471 --> 50:58.430
Byeon Si-on.

51:00.223 --> 51:01.516
Byeon Si-on!

51:14.946 --> 51:18.033
The 46th Korean Film Awards
Best Actress Award goes to…

51:22.621 --> 51:23.789
MY MOTHER, OH JEONG-HUI
AUTUMN SCENES, KANG JI-EUN

51:23.872 --> 51:26.082
Oh Jeong-hui from My Mother.

51:26.166 --> 51:27.417
Congratulations!

51:37.219 --> 51:39.012
BEST ACTRESS AWARD
MY MOTHER, OH JEONG-HUI

51:52.692 --> 51:53.652
Thank you.

51:56.905 --> 52:00.617
They say actors are happy to be on stage,
even if they're just a tree.

52:01.243 --> 52:03.745
I would've been happy just being a tree,

52:03.829 --> 52:07.123
so I find it amazing
that I've gotten this far.

52:07.207 --> 52:10.627
At the same time, another part of me
feels it was inevitable,

52:10.710 --> 52:14.422
as if I've been walking a path
that was already decided.

52:15.632 --> 52:18.426
I'm feeling both emotions so distinctly,

52:19.052 --> 52:21.012
like my heart is split in two.

52:21.763 --> 52:24.724
"This is amazing. How did I get this far?"

52:24.808 --> 52:26.560
"But wasn't it inevitable?"

52:27.936 --> 52:30.397
I also feel joy and fear at the same time.

52:31.815 --> 52:34.609
The joy of achievement.

52:35.694 --> 52:40.198
And the fear that this crown was gained
at the expense of others.

52:40.782 --> 52:42.993
It feels like this came
at the expense of the crew's hard work.

52:44.911 --> 52:45.996
And it feels like…

52:48.623 --> 52:51.042
this came at the expense of the happiness

52:52.752 --> 52:55.046
of my young daughter,
whom I couldn't be there for.

52:57.507 --> 52:59.009
That guilt

53:00.010 --> 53:01.845
led to my regret
over not being able to love Mi-ran

53:03.513 --> 53:05.181
as fully as I wanted.

53:08.643 --> 53:11.187
I approached My Mother

53:11.271 --> 53:15.817
in the hopes of bringing comfort
to mothers like me who carry many regrets,

53:16.401 --> 53:18.486
and to the daughters

53:18.570 --> 53:20.447
who have had to endure imperfect mothers.

53:22.240 --> 53:23.533
I dedicate this great award

53:24.159 --> 53:26.286
to mothers and daughters everywhere

53:26.369 --> 53:28.955
who have gone through difficult times

53:30.123 --> 53:32.626
and who have continued on despite them.

54:28.014 --> 54:29.015
Are you okay?

54:29.641 --> 54:31.726
Let me help you get down. Slowly.

54:37.357 --> 54:39.275
If you could erase your childhood memories

54:39.359 --> 54:41.277
to escape from this pain,

54:43.071 --> 54:44.322
would you do it?

54:48.743 --> 54:49.661
No.

54:51.705 --> 54:54.165
Without this pain, that woman…

54:57.419 --> 54:59.254
would be completely innocent.

55:29.034 --> 55:31.244
I've never gotten an "unknown."

55:32.287 --> 55:34.330
You might not have seen it,

55:34.414 --> 55:35.790
but it showed up twice.

55:37.125 --> 55:39.127
It first appeared on October 29th.

55:42.005 --> 55:43.381
I don't remember it at all.

55:44.007 --> 55:45.550
When "unknown" appears,

55:45.633 --> 55:48.094
one or two minutes
of the situation are recorded

55:48.178 --> 55:51.598
because participants
might not recall the situation.

55:52.515 --> 55:53.850
Would you like to listen to it?

55:55.435 --> 55:59.189
RECORDING

56:01.316 --> 56:02.150
Jin-man.

56:05.028 --> 56:06.321
What are you doing?

56:07.405 --> 56:08.823
Weren't you drinking?

56:10.617 --> 56:11.618
Come down.

56:14.412 --> 56:15.663
It's okay. Come down.

56:19.334 --> 56:20.752
You need to eat something.

56:22.504 --> 56:24.714
I'll make kimchi fried rice, so come down.

56:31.346 --> 56:34.516
And it appeared again recently.

56:35.141 --> 56:36.351
Let's listen to it.

56:38.812 --> 56:41.564
RECORDING

57:07.423 --> 57:08.550
I'm sorry.

57:11.803 --> 57:13.930
What kind of emotion do you think this is?

57:16.724 --> 57:18.143
I'm not sure.

57:20.311 --> 57:22.355
What should I call this?

57:27.152 --> 57:30.572
There's someone else who keeps showing
the same emotion pattern.

57:33.700 --> 57:35.493
Please send me the data for number 38.

57:36.327 --> 57:37.579
I'm number 38.

57:38.288 --> 57:39.289
That's a winning hand.

57:42.125 --> 57:44.085
Let's see, number 38…

57:46.087 --> 57:48.298
This person has trauma
from being abandoned as a child,

57:48.381 --> 57:51.843
so when they encounter similar situations,
they feel this emotion.

57:52.469 --> 57:53.636
They experience it often.

57:53.720 --> 57:55.180
About once or twice a month?

57:57.724 --> 57:58.808
This person

57:59.434 --> 58:02.770
described the feeling
as "self-destructive."

58:03.730 --> 58:05.148
"Self-destructive."

58:12.363 --> 58:13.490
What about you?

58:14.073 --> 58:15.992
How would you describe it?

58:17.869 --> 58:20.580
What kind of emotion would you call this?

58:23.875 --> 58:26.503
Does "self-destructive" feel right?

58:29.130 --> 58:33.134
It's a little different
from typical "anger" or "frustration"

58:33.760 --> 58:37.138
because there's about 7%
of some kind of desperation mixed in.

58:41.726 --> 58:43.311
I can see this is getting hard for you.

58:43.394 --> 58:44.687
Should we continue later?

58:44.771 --> 58:47.023
You can tell me about it later.

58:54.989 --> 58:55.865
"Help me."

59:00.119 --> 59:01.412
It's a cry for help.

59:05.792 --> 59:07.210
The 7% of desperation…

59:09.712 --> 59:10.838
is "help me."

59:13.258 --> 59:14.175
Help me.

59:16.177 --> 59:17.095
Words…

59:19.138 --> 59:20.890
I've never spoken in my life.

59:24.018 --> 59:24.936
Help me.

59:41.035 --> 59:45.873
Do you remember when I said someone else
shared the same pattern as you?

59:47.292 --> 59:48.167
Number 4000.

59:50.003 --> 59:51.713
"Participant number 4000."

59:51.796 --> 59:52.964
What?

59:53.047 --> 59:54.382
Number 4000 out of 4000 people.

59:54.465 --> 59:55.508
You're the last one.

59:56.509 --> 59:59.012
They showed the same pattern as you again.

01:00:00.221 --> 01:00:03.391
It's the same pattern that you exhibit
when you get nosebleeds,

01:00:03.891 --> 01:00:06.436
and this is how they described
the emotion.

01:00:08.438 --> 01:00:09.397
"Help me."

01:00:12.108 --> 01:00:13.401
They said

01:00:14.235 --> 01:00:16.654
it was like a desperate cry for help.

01:00:17.905 --> 01:00:18.865
Do you agree?

01:00:41.971 --> 01:00:43.097
Why does…

01:00:44.974 --> 01:00:46.893
Why does that person feel that way?

01:03:20.880 --> 01:03:21.714
I'll help you.

01:03:29.806 --> 01:03:32.225
We're already helping each other

01:03:34.018 --> 01:03:34.852
a lot.

01:03:46.489 --> 01:03:47.573
We're in sync.

01:03:55.998 --> 01:03:56.916
In sync.

01:04:38.457 --> 01:04:39.292
Let's…

01:04:45.381 --> 01:04:46.299
find Yeong-sil.

01:05:34.430 --> 01:05:36.641
What kind of weather
should I make for you?

01:05:38.643 --> 01:05:40.561
Tell me what kind of weather
you like, Eun-a,

01:05:41.270 --> 01:05:42.438
and I'll make it for you.

01:05:45.316 --> 01:05:46.150
I like

01:05:46.817 --> 01:05:48.277
any kind of wind.

01:07:09.775 --> 01:07:11.152
A happy imagination…

01:07:12.903 --> 01:07:13.779
complete.

01:07:36.469 --> 01:07:38.137
WE ARE ALL TRYING HERE

01:07:56.739 --> 01:07:58.282
You know exactly where I'm stuck

01:07:58.866 --> 01:08:02.286
and where I need to focus emotionally
so I can really take off.

01:08:02.870 --> 01:08:04.163
Is it okay to use "Yeong-sil"

01:08:04.246 --> 01:08:06.123
as my pseudonym?

01:08:06.207 --> 01:08:08.667
I told you I'm not co-writing,
so why'd you set up an appointment?

01:08:09.335 --> 01:08:12.046
You're the funniest director
I've ever met.

01:08:13.339 --> 01:08:15.132
No one our age has this kind of stamina.

01:08:15.216 --> 01:08:17.593
-I never knew work could be so much fun.
-Who likes who exactly?

01:08:18.594 --> 01:08:20.304
Whenever I feel like I'm being abandoned,

01:08:20.387 --> 01:08:22.306
my whole body aches, and I get nosebleeds.

01:08:23.099 --> 01:08:25.142
The first person who wrote me off.

01:08:25.643 --> 01:08:26.519
My mom.

01:08:28.020 --> 01:08:33.025
Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
